! name: gaius web half
! description: Re-ranking for the curate's Brave searches: primary and technical sources up, vendor listicles and product marketing out.
! public: false
! author: zndx
!
! 2026-09-06: the week-first freshness change surfaced ten vendor listicles in
! one curate ("Top 10 AI Tools for Researchers in 2026 | AnswerThis" …), and the
! pipeline dressed them as research briefs. Content engineered to rank for
! research-tool queries is adversarial to the selection function; it is
! discarded at acquisition, before it can be summarised. Passed inline as the
! `goggles` parameter by _fetch_brave (config/brave/web-half.goggle, tracked with
! `git add -f`). Rules: pattern$action,option — see github.com/brave/goggles-quickstart.

! --- structural marketing patterns (URL) ---
/best/$discard
/best-$discard
/top-$discard
/top/$discard
-tools$discard
-tools/$discard
/tools/$discard
/alternatives$discard
/pricing$discard
/compare$discard
/comparison$discard
/vs-$discard
/review$discard
/reviews$discard

! --- index and search pages are not sources ---
/list/$discard
/search$discard
/tag/$discard
/category/$discard

! --- vendors and content farms seen on the surface (2026-09-02..06) ---
$discard,site=answerthis.io
$discard,site=agentic.ai
$discard,site=lindy.ai
$discard,site=jenni.ai
$discard,site=buffer.com
$discard,site=hootsuite.com
$discard,site=peoplemanagingpeople.com
$discard,site=document360.com
$discard,site=zendesk.com
$discard,site=martech.org
$discard,site=magai.co
$discard,site=aicontentfy.com
$discard,site=wprssaggregator.com

! --- primary and technical sources ---
/abs/$boost=2,site=arxiv.org
/html/$boost=2,site=arxiv.org
/pdf/$boost=1,site=arxiv.org
$boost=2,site=doi.org
$boost=1,site=dl.acm.org
$boost=1,site=ieeexplore.ieee.org
$boost=1,site=nature.com
$boost=1,site=sciencedirect.com
$boost=1,site=link.springer.com
$boost=1,site=openreview.net
$boost=1,site=github.com
